To a point.  I normally play a monk using marial arts and a
crossbow, at least at the start.  I also normally pray more than
I sacrifice, sacrificing mainly to find out if it is safe to
pray.  When one of those sacrifices, early in the game, gave me
Grayswandir, however, I wasn't afraid to change tactics.
Consider it a sign or an omen, if you wish, but that Monk got a
good deal further than any other monk I've played.

This sort of leads to another point: why is it that when you're
sacrificing like crazy, trying to get an artifact, they never
come, but when you're sacrificing only to be sure that it's safe
to pray, you very often get an artifact?

